# cmake/oauth.local.cmake.example
#
# A build machine's private OAuth settings, kept out of the repository.
#
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this file to cmake/oauth.local.cmake (that name is gitignored).
#   2. Set the sign-in service this build should use (below).
#   3. Reconfigure the build (cmake ...). The top-level CMakeLists.txt includes
#      this file automatically when present.
#
# UltraMail and UltraCloud carry no OAuth client id or secret: they sign in to
# Google, Microsoft, Yahoo and Dropbox through the ULTRA OS sign-in service
# (Server/OAuthCallback), which holds the registrations and receives the
# providers' redirects. The address is built into UltraNet
# (UltraCanvas/CMakeLists.txt, ULTRANET_OAUTH_SERVICE_URL); the default is the
# public one, and a private deployment names its own here. Empty = no built-in
# service: such a build signs in only with what is configured at run time (a
# service named by ULTRANET_OAUTH_SERVICE_URL or an oauth.ini's [service] url,
# or a client of the installation's own - see Docs/UltraMail/AccountSetup.md,
# section 3).
#
# This overrides nothing at run time: UltraNet_OAuth2SetSignInService(), the
# environment and the INI file all still take priority.

set(ULTRANET_OAUTH_SERVICE_URL "https://oauth-callback.ultraos.eu" CACHE STRING "" FORCE)
